@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Overview";
}

<section class="welcome" aria-labelledby="welcome-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your access workspace</p>
    <h1 id="welcome-title">Your UNO.<br />Your access rules.</h1>
    <p class="intro">Choose an active policy and set how fingerprint and PIN access should work on your bench UNO.</p>
    <a class="primary-link" asp-page="/Policies/Index">Manage access policies <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</section>

<section id="devices" class="device-panel" aria-labelledby="devices-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">PoC device overview</p>
            <h2 id="devices-title">Bench device</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="status-label">Connection status not tracked</span>
    </div>
    <div class="empty-state">
        <div class="device-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="sensor"></span><span class="indicator"></span>
        </div>
        <h3>Arduino UNO R4 WiFi</h3>
        <p>A configured bench device fetches its active policy.<br class="desktop-break" />
            Fingerprint matching and PIN verification happen on the UNO.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-note">Provision the same registration key on the portal and UNO before using PIN policies. Device registration and check-in tracking are not implemented.</div>
</section>

<section class="roadmap" aria-labelledby="roadmap-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="roadmap-title">Your access workspace</h2>
        <span class="muted">One step at a time</span>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <h3>Bench key setup</h3>
            <p>Local setup provisions a shared PIN-verification key on the portal and UNO. Device registration is planned for a future update.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <h3>Access policies</h3>
            <p>Create policies and make them available through the policy API. <a asp-page="/Policies/Index">Manage your policies</a>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <h3>Activity</h3>
            <p>Device check-in history and access events are planned for a future update.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
